--- log ---
2026-06-02T16:44Z claude created
2026-06-02T23:30Z claude note design council revised the pre-PUSH mechanism from "autoarchive (move files)" to "warn-only". A pre-push hook receives the already-frozen ref set and runs before the push leaves; any os.Rename + commit it makes lands one push LATER, never in the gated push -- so the literal "move at pre-push" is technically unreachable. Worse, a mutating pre-push hook leaves an uncommitted move that git reset --hard / stash / git add -A can resurrect into a ticket present in BOTH tickets/ and tickets/closed/ (a reopened/duplicate ticket). The faithful realization of the charter intent (mechanize/surface archiving at push, zero convention) is therefore: the hook WARNS (names closed-but-unarchived tickets + prints the exact archive+commit+push recipe), mutates nothing, exits 0. The real archive remains at merge time (erg-pr-merge already runs erg close + erg archive) and via manual erg archive. Exit criteria below reworded accordingly. Also: verify is CI-fail-closed (could-not-verify in GITHUB_ACTIONS -> exit 1) but lenient locally; pre-push goes behind its own --push-hook flag (0208 promised "each piece of wiring requires an explicit opt-in flag"). Blocker #1 -> option (b) standalone script + stderr dispatch hint. Blocker #2 -> doc-only + regression test (no fragile pre-commit env sniff).

2026-06-02T22:14Z MinhHaDuong closed — autoclosed — PR #244
--- body ---
## Context

Cf. docs/erg-imagine-charter.md, chantiers 7 et 8.

Executer apres 0208 (install --hooks/--inject-agents).

Ce ticket couvre la couche forge `erg-github` (deux verbes : `install`,
`verify`) et le mecanisme d'autoarchive par hook pre-PUSH. Il inclut
la decision de dispatch (blocker #1), la portabilite/degradation gracieuse,
et le check CI P2 "enforce" qui remplace l'idee d'un autoclose-bot.

Principe : erg core ne depend jamais d'erg-github (contrat offline preserve).
Le close est erg core ; le discover est erg-github ; le land est l'auteur.

## Blockers transverses

- #1 -- Dispatch `erg-github` non specifie. Trancher : (a) dispatch
  git-style dans main.go (commande inconnue -> chercher erg-foo sur PATH,
  --help liste les helpers decouverts), ou (b) script separe documente +
  erreur actionnable si on tape `erg github`. Decision a figer ici.
- #2 -- Archive en pre-PUSH, pas pre-commit. erg archive fait os.Rename ;
  en pre-commit le fichier deplace n'est pas re-stage. Le hook pre-PUSH
  evite le probleme. Interdire explicitement erg archive en pre-commit.
- #5 -- Checklist sous-commande (si dispatch option a retenu).

## Travail

1. Creer `tickets/erg-github` (POSIX sh). Deux verbes :
   - `install` : pose le YAML d'Actions (check CI requis pre-merge).
   - `verify` : discover forge via `gh` -> pass/fail.

2. Hook pre-PUSH autoarchive : balaye les tickets clos pas-encore-ranges,
   deplace vers closed/, imprime ce qu'il a deplace.

3. Degradation gracieuse : si `gh` absent ou non-authentifie,
   `erg-github verify` sort avec un message clair et un code non-bloquant.

4. Echappatoire : le check CI passe si la PR ne reference aucun ticket.

## Surfaces

Code :
- `tickets/erg-github` (nouveau script POSIX sh : install + verify)
- `src/go/install.go` (nouveau flag --push-hook + planPushHook : bloc pre-push
  WARN-ONLY, reutilise resolveHooksDir/stripManagedRegions/insert/atomicWrite)
- `src/go/archive.go` (nouveau --dry-run : WOULD ARCHIVE, ne renomme rien)
- `src/go/main.go` (hint dispatch : cmd=="github" -> erreur actionnable stderr)
- `src/go/helptext.go` (helpArchive --dry-run ; helpInstall --push-hook)

Tests :
- `tests/test_erg_github.sh` (nouveau : verify echec, succes, degradation)
- `tests/test_install.sh` (hook pre-PUSH archive end-to-end)
- `tests/test_docs.sh` (compte de sections si dispatch ajoute)
- `Makefile` TEST_SUITES

Docs :
- README.md (pointeur vers erg-github)
- src/go/assets/AGENTS.md, src/go/assets/integration.md (mention)
- CONTRIBUTING.md (politique scripts commites)

CI :
- `.github/workflows/` (le YAML que erg-github install pose)

## Derisque

- Degradation gracieuse : gh absent -> message clair, code non-bloquant.
- Echappatoire : PR sans reference ticket -> check passe (merge d'urgence).
- Portabilite : POSIX sh de preference a bash.
- Pre-commit interdit pour archive (blocker #2) : guard ou message.
- Binaire commite : decider si la regle pre-commit "rejet binaire hors
  main" s'applique a erg-github.

## Exit criteria (revised per design council -- see 2026-06-02 log)

- [ ] Dispatch tranche : option (b) script separe ; `erg github` imprime une
      erreur actionnable nommant tickets/erg-github (stderr, exit 1). Pas de
      dispatch git-style PATH-exec, pas de section --help (compte reste 19).
- [ ] tickets/erg-github commite, executable (mode 100755), en POSIX sh
      (#!/bin/sh, set -eu, aucun bashisme).
- [ ] erg-github install pose .github/workflows/erg-verify.yml epingle :
      on: pull_request sans filtre paths ; permissions contents:read +
      pull-requests:read ; checkout ref head.sha ; verify avec GH_TOKEN.
- [ ] erg-github verify echoue (exit 1) si la PR reference un ticket non-ferme.
- [ ] erg-github verify passe (exit 0) si la PR ne reference aucun ticket
      (echappatoire LOUD et distincte : "no ticket referenced (escape hatch)").
- [ ] erg-github verify : degradation environnement-dependante. Hors CI
      (gh absent / non-auth / pas de PR) -> exit 0 (non-bloquant local). En CI
      (GITHUB_ACTIONS) un could-not-verify -> exit 1 LOUD (fail-closed : un
      check requis vert qui n'a pas pu tourner n'enforce rien).
- [ ] erg-github verify : >1 reference Ticket: -> exit 1 ("one PR closes one
      ticket") ; extraction parite avec erg-pr-merge (anchored, insensible a
      la casse, 0-2 asterisques), sed/grep portable (pas de grep -oP GNU-only).
- [ ] Hook pre-PUSH (pose par `erg install --push-hook`, flag OPT-IN distinct
      de --hooks) AVERTIT des tickets clos-pas-ranges (nomme + recette
      archive+commit+push), NE MUTE RIEN, exit 0 (jamais bloquant).
- [ ] `erg archive --dry-run` : meme scan, imprime "WOULD ARCHIVE <file>" /
      SKIPPED-blocked, ne renomme rien, exit 0. (Surface de lecture requise
      par le hook ; archive.go rejette tout flag aujourd'hui.)
- [ ] erg archive interdit en pre-commit : doc explicite + test de regression
      asserant que le bloc pre-commit (hookBody) ne contient jamais "archive".
      Pas de guard runtime (un sniff d'env pre-commit est fragile).
- [ ] README pointe vers erg-github (et note l'echappatoire advisory-with-audit).
- [ ] AGENTS.md et integration.md mentionnent erg-github ; integration.md
      Uninstall couvre le bloc pre-push.
- [ ] Regle binaire : `^tickets/erg$` exact ; tickets/erg-github (script texte)
      committable sur toute branche (test de non-rejet).
- [ ] Tests : verify echec/succes/no-ref/gh-absent/multi-ref ; push-hook non
      bloquant (binaire absent, rien en attente, et avertit+exit0 si pending) ;
      YAML epingle ; mode 100755 ; portabilite (pas de bashisme).
- [ ] `make test` + `erg check tickets/` passent (il n'y a pas de cible
      `make check` ; la porte est make test + erg check).
